:Class TableViewer
⍝ = Overview
⍝ This class is designed to display tables. For editing tables see `TableEdit`.
⍝ You can modify the Form and its children to some extend by setting the `modalWait` parameter to 0.
⍝ That will create the Form and the Grid but does not dequeue it. At that point you can, say, add _
⍝ a menubar to it.
⍝ = Limitations
⍝ `TableViewer` is not a general cover for the Dyalog Grid control: `TableTableViewer` assumes the _
⍝ all columns have a single data type. That's what you get when you read data from a SQL database.
⍝ Also, the number of rows and particularly columns should be reasonable: though a table may have _
⍝ thousands of rows and hundred or so columns, it's not designed for tables with millions of rows _
⍝ and / or thousands of columns.

⍝ Author: Kai Jaeger

    :Include APLGuiUtils

    ⎕IO←0 ⋄ ⎕ML←3

    :Field Public Shared ReadOnly InactiaveColor←128 128 128

    ∇ r←ListHelpers
      :Access Public Shared
      r←'CreateGrid' 'Edit' 'Browse'
    ∇

    ∇ {n}←{x}Run table;⎕TRAP;globalParms;parms;parms2
      :Access Public Shared
      ⎕TRAP←(APLGuiError'E'('⎕DMX.EM ⎕SIGNAL ',⍕APLGuiError))(0 'N')
      'Invalid table - columns must have a single data type'⎕SIGNAL 11/⍨∨/1≠↑¨⍴¨∪¨↓⍉' '=↑¨1↑¨0⍴¨table
      x←{(0<⎕NC ⍵):⍎⍵ ⋄ ⍬}'x'
      (globalParms parms)←CreateParms GetParms x
      parms.readonly←1
      parms2←##.StdForm.CreateParms
      parms2.(posn size)←parms.(posn size)
      parms2.addToCaption←parms.addToCaption
      n←##.StdForm.Create globalParms parms2
      n.menubar←##.Menubar.Create n.∆Form parms.menu ⍬(⎕NEW ##.KeyCodes)
      n.menubar.⎕DF'[Menubar namespace]:Menubar'
      parms.parent←n.∆Form
      n.Grid←globalParms CreateGrid parms table
      n.StatusField1.Text←(⍕0⊃⍴table),' x ',⍕1⊃⍴table
      :If parms.modalWait
          ⎕DQ n.∆Form
          n←⍬
      :EndIf
    ∇

    ∇ {n}←{globalParms}CreateGrid(parms table);⎕TRAP
      :Access Public Shared
      ⎕TRAP←(APLGuiError'E'('⎕DMX.EM ⎕SIGNAL ',⍕APLGuiError))(0 'N')
      'Invalid table - columns must have a single data type'⎕SIGNAL 11/⍨∨/1≠↑¨⍴¨∪¨↓⍉' '=↑¨1↑¨0⍴¨table
      'Missing parameter: "parent"'⎕SIGNAL 11/⍨¯1≡parms.parent
      n←⎕NS''
      globalParms←{(0<⎕NC ⍵):⍎⍵ ⋄ ⍬}'globalParms'
      (globalParms parms)←CreateParms GetParms globalParms parms
      parms.readonly←1
      parms←CheckGridParms parms
      n←CreateGridAndStuffForBrowse n parms globalParms table
      n.Grid.Values←table
      {}SetColSize n
    ∇

    ∇ r←CreateParms
      :Access Public Shared
    ⍝ Returns a namespace with default values for creating a form via a call to `Table.CreateGrid`.
    ⍝ Note that all other (more specialized) `CreateParmsFor*` funtions call this one first, then add _
    ⍝ add new or modify existing ones.
    ⍝ || ''Parameter name'' ||''Comment''||
    ⍝ || `addToCaption` || Together with the "caption" this is used to compile the caption.||
    ⍝ || `cellWidths`   || Defaults to ⍬. Can be scalar or a vector instead. Vector length must match number of columns in table.||
    ⍝ || `colTitles`    || Defaults to `''`. Can be scalar or a vector instead. Vector length must match number of columns in table.||
    ⍝ || `datatypes`    || Defaults to ⍬. Can be scalar or a vector instead. Vector length must match number of columns in table. See `Enums.TableDataTypes`. ||
    ⍝ || `decimals`     || Defaults to 0. Can be scalar or a vector instead. Vector length must match number of columns in table.||
    ⍝ || `fontInput`    || Font to be used inside the table.||
    ⍝ || `modalWait`    || Boolean that defaults to 1. A 1 will make `Browse` dequeue the Form. Useful for adding a menubar etc.||
    ⍝ || `size`         || Defaults to `(⍬ ⍬)`. Set this to a two-item vector in case you want the Form to have a certain size.||
    ⍝ || `parent`       || Form or SubForm hosting the grid. Defaults to n.∆Form if not specified.||
    ⍝ || `parmsType`    || Must be "BrowseTable".||
    ⍝ || `posn`         || Defaults to `(⍬ ⍬)`. Use this to specify a certain position for the Form.||
    ⍝ || `rowTitles`    || Defaults to rows numbered from 1. Use 0 to suppress row titles. Otherwise it must be a vector of text vectors matching the table cols.||
      r←##.APLGuiParameterSpace.Create
      r.addToCaption←''
      r.cellWidths←⍬
      r.colTitles←''
      r.dataTypes←⍬
      r.decimals←⍬
      r.fontInput←¯1
      r.modalWait←1
      r.menu←GetBrowseMenu ⍬
      r.size←⍬ ⍬
      r.parent←¯1
      r.parmType←'BrowseTable'
      r.posn←⍬ ⍬
      r.rowTitles←¯1
     ⍝Done
    ∇

⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝ Private

    ∇ {parms}←CheckGridParms parms
      parms.rowTitles{⍵:'' ⋄ ⍺}←¯1≡parms.rowTitles
    ∇

    ∇ n←CreateGridAndStuffForBrowse(n parms globalParms table);bool;dt
      n←CreateBrowseGrid n parms globalParms table
      :If 0=≢parms.dataTypes
          parms.dataTypes←(##.Enums.TableDataTypes.(Numeric Char))[↑¨' '=1↑¨0⍴¨table[0;]]
      :EndIf
      n←CreateInputControls n parms 1
      :If 0∊parms.dataTypes∊##.Enums.TableDataTypes.∆List[;1]
          11 ⎕SIGNAL⍨'Invalid data types'
      :EndIf
      n.Grid.Input.Bcol←⊂3⍴230
      n.Grid.CellTypes←(⍴table)⍴1+⍳1⊃⍴table
      n.Grid.onContextMenu←'OnContextMenu'
      n.Grid.onGridKeyPress←'OnGridKeyPress'parms.readonly
    ∇

    ∇ n←CreateBrowseGrid(n parms globalParms table);∆;bool;dt
      ∆←''
      ∆,←⊂'Coord' 'Prop'
      ∆,←⊂'Posn'(0 0)
      ∆,←⊂'Size'(100 100)
      ∆,←⊂'BCol'(⊂230 230 230)
      :If ¯1≢parms.fontInput
          ∆,←⊂'Font'parms.fontInput
      :Else
          ∆,←⊂'Font'globalParms.fontInput
      :EndIf
      ∆,←{0=≢⍵:'' ⋄ ⊂'CellWidths'⍵}parms.cellWidths
      ∆,←{0=≢⍵:'' ⋄ ⊂'ColTitlesWidths'⍵}parms.cellWidths
      :If 0≠≢parms.rowTitles
          :If (,0)≡,parms.rowTitles
              ∆,←⊂'TitleWidth' 0
          :Else
              ∆,←⊂'RowTitles'parms.rowTitles
          :EndIf
      :EndIf
      n.Grid←parms.parent.⎕NEW'Grid'∆
      n.Grid.⎕DF'[Grid]:Grid'
      n.Grid.Coord←'Pixel'  ⍝ For GetTextSize
      n.Grid.ShowInput←1
      n.Grid.ColTitles←parms.colTitles
      n.Grid.ResizeCols←1
      n.Grid.EnterReadOnlyCells←1
     ⍝Done
    ∇

    ∇ {n}←CreateInputControls(n parms browseFlag);∆;dataType;e;i;inputControls
    ⍝ Note that the sequence in which the controls are created IS important:
    ⍝ It has to be in sync with what ##.Enums.TableDataTypes.∆List returns,
    ⍝ and that will be alphabetically sorted.
      e←##.Enums.TableDataTypes
      inputControls←⍬   ⍝ Collect and assigned later to Grid.Input to circumvent Dyalog bug <00964>
      :For i :In ⍳≢parms.dataTypes
          dataType←i⊃parms.dataTypes
          :Select dataType
          :Case e.Bool
              inputControls,←i CreateInputControl_Bool n browseFlag
          :Case e.Char
              inputControls,←i CreateInputControl_Char n browseFlag
          :Case e.Currency
              inputControls,←i CreateInputControl_Currency n browseFlag parms
          :Case e.Date
              inputControls,←i CreateInputControl_Date n browseFlag
          :Case e.Numeric
              inputControls,←i CreateInputControl_Numeric n browseFlag parms
          :Case e.Time
              inputControls,←i CreateInputControl_Time n browseFlag
          :Else
              . ⍝ Huuh?!
          :EndSelect
      :EndFor
      n.Grid.Input←inputControls
    ∇

    ∇ {ref}←i CreateInputControl_Char(n readOnly);∆;ref
    ⍝ Creates two controls, one for editing & one just for browsing.
      :If readOnly
          ref←n.Grid.⎕NEW'Label'(,⊂'FieldType' 'Char')
      :Else
          ref←n.Grid.⎕NEW'Edit'(,⊂'FieldType' 'Char')
      :EndIf
      {}n AssignRefToColumn i ref
    ∇

    ∇ {ref}←i CreateInputControl_Numeric(n readOnly parms);∆;ref
    ⍝ Creates two controls, one for editing & one just for browsing.
      ∆←''
      ∆,←⊂'FieldType' 'Numeric'
      ∆,←⊂'ValidIfEmpty' 1
      ∆,←⊂'Decimals'(i{⍺∊⍵:i⊃⍵ ⋄ 0}parms.decimals)
      ∆,←readOnly/⊂'ReadOnly' 1
      ref←n.Grid.⎕NEW'Edit'∆
      ref.⎕DF'[Numeric_Edit]'
      {}n AssignRefToColumn i ref
    ∇

    ∇ {ref}←i CreateInputControl_Currency(n readOnly parms);∆;ref
    ⍝ Creates two controls, one for editing & one just for browsing.
      ∆←''
      ∆,←⊂'FieldType' 'Currency'
      ∆,←⊂'ValidIfEmpty' 1
      ∆,←⊂'Decimals'({0=≢⍵:2 ⋄ ⍵}i{i<≢⍵:i⊃⍵ ⋄ 2}parms.decimals)
      ∆,←readOnly/⊂'ReadOnly' 1
      ref←n.Grid.⎕NEW'Edit'∆
      ref.⎕DF'[Currency_Edit]'
      {}n AssignRefToColumn i ref
    ∇

    ∇ {ref}←i CreateInputControl_Date(n readOnly);∆;ref
    ⍝ Creates two controls, one for editing & one just for browsing.
      ∆←''
      ∆,←⊂'FieldType' 'Char'
      ∆,←⊂'FormatString' 'ZI4,<->,ZI2,<->,ZI2'
      ∆,←⊂'ValidIfEmpty' 1
      ∆,←readOnly/⊂'ReadOnly' 1
      ref←n.Grid.⎕NEW'Edit'∆
      ref.⎕DF'[Char_Edit]'
      {}n AssignRefToColumn i ref
    ∇

    ∇ {ref}←i CreateInputControl_Time(n readOnly);∆;ref
    ⍝ Creates two controls, one for editing & one just for browsing.
      ∆←''
      ∆,←⊂'FieldType' 'Time'
      ∆,←readOnly/⊂'ReadOnly' 1
      ref←n.Grid.⎕NEW'Edit'∆
      ref.⎕DF'[Time_Edit]'
      {}n AssignRefToColumn i ref
    ∇

    ∇ {ref}←i CreateInputControl_Bool(n readOnly);∆;ref
    ⍝ Creates two controls, one for editing & one just for browsing.
      ∆←''
      ∆,←⊂'Caption' 'Yes/No'
      ∆,←⊂'Style' 'Check'
      ∆,←⊂'BCol'(140 140 140)
      :If readOnly
          ∆,←⊂'Active' 0
          ∆,←⊂'BCol' 0
      :EndIf
      ref←n.Grid.⎕NEW'Button'∆
      ref.⎕DF'[YesNo_Edit]'
      {}n AssignRefToColumn i ref
    ∇

    :Section InActive

    ∇ {ref}←i CreateInputControl_DropEdit(n readOnly);∆;ref
    ⍝ Creates two controls, one for editing & one just for browsing.
      . ⍝ not ready yet  ⍝TODO⍝
      ∆←''
      ∆,←⊂'Style' 'Drop'
      ∆,←⊂'Style' 'DropEdit'
      ∆,←readOnly/⊂'Active' 0
      ref←n.Grid.⎕NEW'Combo'∆
      ref.⎕DF'[DropEdit_Edit]'
      n AssignRefToColumn i ref
    ∇

    ∇ {ref}←i CreateInputControl_Drop(n readOnly);∆;ref
    ⍝ Creates two controls, one for editing & one just for browsing.
      . ⍝ not ready yet  ⍝TODO⍝
      ∆←''
      ∆,←⊂'Style' 'Drop'
      ∆,←readOnly/⊂'Active' 0
      ref←n.Grid.⎕NEW'Combo'∆
      ref.⎕DF'[DropDownt]'
      n AssignRefToColumn i ref
    ∇

    :EndSection

      DetermineColumnDataTypes←{
     ⍝ Returns the proper definition for a single row depending on parms.dataTypes and _
     ⍝ ##.Enums.TableDataTypes
          (n parms)←⍵
          ind←{(≢⍵)⍴⍳≢⍵}##.Enums.TableDataTypes.∆List
          rows←##.Enums.TableDataTypes.∆List[;1]⍳parms.dataTypes
          r←(rows,¨parms.readonly)⌷¨⊂ind
          r
      }

    ∇ {r}←SetInputModeTo type
      r←⍬
      :Select type
      :Case 'Scroll'
          'Grid'⎕WS('InputMode' 'Scroll')('Cursor' 0)
      :Case 'AlwaysInCell'
          'Grid'⎕WS('InputMode' 'AlwaysInCell')('Cursor' 3)
      :EndSelect
    ∇

      GetRefTo_n←{
     ⍝ ⍵ is a ref pointing to any control.
     ⍝ If that is a Form that it will contain an "n" namepsace, and that is returned.
     ⍝ If that is not the case then we climb up one step and try again
          'Form'≡⍵.Type:⍵.n
          ∇ ⍵.##
      }

      AssignRefToColumn←{
          (i ref)←⍵
          n←⍺
          _←⍎'≢n.col_',(¯3↑'000',(⍕i)),'←ref'
          n
      }

      CreateContextMenuForBrowse←{
          n←⍵
          n2←⎕NS''
          n2.Menu←n.Grid.⎕NEW⊂'Menu'
          n2.Cancel←n2.Menu.⎕NEW'MenuItem'(⊂('Caption' 'Cancel'))
          c2.Cancel.⎕DF'[MenuItem]:Cancel'
          n2.Cancel.onSelect←1
          n2.sep1←n2.Menu.⎕NEW⊂'Separator'
          n2.Copy←n2.Menu.⎕NEW'MenuItem'(('Caption'('Copy',(⎕UCS 9),'Ctrl+C'))('Accelerator'(67 2)))
          c2.Copy.⎕DF'[MenuItem]:Copy'
          n2.Copy.onSelect←1
          n2
      }

      GetBrowseMenu←{
          r←''
          r,←⊂'[File]                                 {File}'
          r,←⊂' Quit=Alt+F4        : OnQuit           {Quit}'
          r,←⊂'[Edit]                                 {Edit}'
          r,←⊂' Copy=Ctrl+C        : OnCopyTable      {Copy}            ;Copies the current selection to the clipboard'
          r,←⊂' -'
          r,←⊂' Select all=Ctrl+A  : OnSelectAll      {SelectAll}       ;Selects all rows and all columns of the table'
          r
      }

      SetColSize←{
    ⍝ For large tables the `SetColSize` method might be (too) slow.
    ⍝ In that case you need to specify the column size via parms.
          n←⍵
          _←{n.Grid.SetColSize ⍵ ¯3}¨⍳1+1⊃⍴n.Grid.Values
          ⍬
      }


⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝⍝ Handler

      OnContextMenu←{
          n←GetRefTo_n↑⍵
          n2←CreateContextMenuForBrowse n
          ans←⎕DQ n2.Menu
          n2.Cancel≡↑ans:⍬
          _←2 ⎕NQ n.Grid.Grid'KeyPress' 'CP' 3 67 2
          ⍬
      }

      OnGridKeyPress←{
          key←2⊃⍵
          ∧/⍺:~(⊂key)∊'DI' 'PT'  ⍝ Ignore the DEL key as well as the "Insert clipboard" key in case the full table is read-only
          0∊⍺:.  ⍝TODO⍝    not completely read-only - we need to check whether it tries in insert/delete protected columns
          1
      }

    ∇ {r}←OnSelectAll msg;n
      :Access Public Shared
      r←0
      n←GetRefTo_n↑msg
      n.Grid.Grid.SelItems←(0 0)(⍴n.Grid.Grid.Values)
    ∇

    ∇ {r}←OnCopyTable msg;n
      :Access Public Shared
      r←0
      n←GetRefTo_n↑msg
      2 ⎕NQ n.Grid.Grid'KeyPress' 'CP' ⍝
    ∇

:EndClass
